# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Every service Dockerfile uses the REPOSITORY ROOT as its build context (a
# Gradle multi-project build cannot be built from a single module directory), so
# this one file governs the context for all of them.
#
# Two reasons this matters beyond image size:
#   1. Copying a host `build/` or `.gradle/` directory into the build stage lets
#      stale, host-JDK-compiled output leak into the image and silently win.
#   2. `infra/secrets/` holds the dev JWT signing keystore. A private key must
#      never enter a build context - it survives in the image history even if a
#      later layer deletes it.
# =============================================================================

# --- build output / tool caches ---------------------------------------------
**/build/
**/out/
**/bin/
**/target/
.gradle/
**/.gradle/

# --- secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
infra/secrets/
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
**/*.pem
**/*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- VCS / IDE / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
**/*.iml
**/.DS_Store

# --- not needed to build a service -------------------------------------------
# NOTE: We need apps/product-catalog and apps/admin-product-catalog for Docker builds
# Exclude only backend service build artifacts, not the frontend source
docs/
.claude/
**/node_modules/
**/*.md
!README.md

# Backend service build artifacts
services/*/build/
services/*/target/
libs/*/build/
libs/*/target/
